  "FINDINGS": {
    "sub_phase_template_trade_reference": "NOT PRESENT. The live \"Sub-phase Template\" list has NO Trade or TradeId column at all -- the connector row carries only Title, SubPhaseNumber, Sequence, DurationDays, DefaultCrew (plus system fields). The expected shape (Trade object + Trade#Id sibling) does NOT hold because the field does not exist on this list. Any downstream flow (Tasks 5-7) that assumes a Trade lookup on Sub-phase Template must either add that column first or source trade-per-subphase from elsewhere (e.g. Crew-Trades intersect, or DefaultCrew).",
    "task_template_subphase_reference": "CONFIRMED. Task Template rows carry SubPhase as {\"@odata.type\":\"#Microsoft.Azure.Connectors.SharePoint.SPListExpandedReference\",\"Id\":<int>,\"Value\":\"<title>\"} plus a sibling scalar \"SubPhase#Id\":<int>. Matches the expected shape exactly. Use item()?['SubPhase#Id'] or item()?['SubPhase']?['Id'] to join -- never Title/Value.",
    "work_calendar_date_column": "Key is \"Date\", a bare date-only string with no time component, e.g. \"2026-08-30\" (matches the DateOnly storage convention already documented in CLAUDE.md). Work Calendar rows also carry a \"Reason\" lookup ({Id, Value} + sibling \"Reason#Id\") that was not called out in the brief but is present and follows the same lookup-reference pattern as SubPhase."
  }
